<section class="sec alt rvl" id="itx-faq">
<div class="wrap">
<div class="sechead">
<div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--violet)">Questions people ask</div>
<h2>Water damage repair FAQ</h2>
</div>
<div class="faq" id="itx-faqlist">
<div class="q"><button aria-expanded="true">Should I put my phone in rice? <svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button>
<div class="a"><div><p>No. Rice doesn't draw water out of a phone, and it can leave dust and starch in the ports. Switch the phone off, dry the outside with a lint-free cloth and bring it in.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="q"><button aria-expanded="false">Can a water damaged phone be fixed? <svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button>
<div class="a"><div><p>Often, yes, but it depends on the liquid, how long the phone was wet and whether it was switched on. The free diagnostic tells you what can be saved before any repair work starts, and if we can't fix it you pay nothing.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="q"><button aria-expanded="false">Can you recover my photos if the phone won't turn on? <svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button>
<div class="a"><div><p>Often, yes. Data recovery is a separate paid service with a free assessment, so you know the options before you decide.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="q"><button aria-expanded="false">My phone is water resistant. Why did it get damaged? <svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button>
<div class="a"><div><p>Water resistance is not waterproofing. The seals weaken with age, drops and heat, and sugary or salty liquid can get past them. That is why a wet phone should be switched off and checked.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="q"><button aria-expanded="false">Do I need an appointment? <svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button>
<div class="a"><div><p>No. Walk in to Bloomsbury or Moorgate any day of the week. Booking is optional.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="q"><button aria-expanded="false">Do you repair tablets with water damage? <svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button>
<div class="a"><div><p>Yes. We repair water damaged iPads and Android tablets at both our Bloomsbury and Moorgate shops. See our <a href="/tablet-repairs/">tablet repairs</a>.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="q"><button aria-expanded="false">Is there a warranty? <svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button>
<div class="a"><div><p>Yes. Every repair carries a warranty on the part and the labour. The period depends on the repair, and we confirm it before any work starts.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
<p style="margin-top:18px">More detail: <a href="/can-water-damaged-phones-recover/">can a water damaged phone recover?</a> and <a href="/phone-corrosion-after-water-damage/">phone corrosion after water damage</a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
